Backlog tail, Selected item/items:

2. Route all MDR filelist entries through a unified shaper processing step that performs §NN§ placeholder substitution (by extension) before truncation
    [ ] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/content_shaper.py': Add extension-aware placeholder substitution as a pre-step within the shaper's processing pass
        - expand the shaper's entry point to accept the filename (or File entity) alongside content and truncation spec
        - check filename against a recognized set of extensions (e.g. `.output-template`)
        - if extension matches: apply a fixed lookup map replacing §01§, §02§, §03§… with the current e.Delims token values
        - if extension does not match: content passes through unchanged (no-op), only truncation applies
        - placeholder tokens use §NN§ form so they cannot collide with active e.Delims values (¤, 🔖, 🗃️, etc.)
        - substitution runs before truncation so from_line / up_to / tail_lines operate on final text
    [ ] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py': Update _res_multi_doc to pass file_obj.name (or the File entity) into the shaper call
        - existing self.shaper.apply_truncation(raw_content, file_obj.truncation_spec) becomes the unified processing call with filename context
        - no structural change to dispatch; every filelist entry already flows through the shaper, this just widens what that pass does
