VI. finished stuffs

1. Expand Delims vocabulary: 4 distinct symbol constants per bookend type
    [x] 'content/backend/core/core/entities.py': Declare 4 separate constants for FILESET and 4 for FILELIST (manifest: TBD, leave as-is for now)
        - FILESET_START_OPEN, FILESET_START_CLOSE, FILESET_END_OPEN, FILESET_END_CLOSE
        - FILELIST_START_OPEN, FILELIST_START_CLOSE, FILELIST_END_OPEN, FILELIST_END_CLOSE
        - initial values can all be "¤" (preserving current wire format), but they are *distinct fields* so any one can be swapped independently
        - PROMPT_SECTION: currently "¤¤" — split to PROMPT_OPEN + PROMPT_CLOSE if desired, or leave as single constant
        - prohibition: do not consolidate into a single shared token; the whole point is per-position independence
    [x] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py': Align _res_multi_doc and _res_repo_content to reference the 4-symbol constants
        - _res_multi_doc (filelist): `FILELIST_START_OPEN name FILELIST_START_CLOSE\n{content}\nFILELIST_END_OPEN name FILELIST_END_CLOSE`
        - _res_repo_content (fileset): `FILESET_START_OPEN path FILESET_START_CLOSE\n{content}\nFILESET_END_OPEN path FILESET_END_CLOSE`
        - _res_manifest: leave as-is or update to a manifest 4-set (low priority)
        - section headers: `PROMPT_OPEN {section} PROMPT_CLOSE` (if split)
    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_parser.py': Align _bookend_re and the closing-bookend string builder to the 4-symbol FILESET constants
        - regex: `^FILESET_START_OPEN\s*(create|update|delete)\s*:\s*(.+?)\s*FILESET_START_CLOSE$`
        - closing bookend string: `f"{FILESET_END_OPEN} {action}: {path} {FILESET_END_CLOSE}"`
    [x] 'content/test/ingestion/code_ingestion_parser_tests.py': Refactor raw-string fixtures to compose from e.Delims constants rather than hardcoding "¤" literals
        - build bookend strings from FILESET_START_OPEN/CLOSE, FILESET_END_OPEN/CLOSE so fixtures stay in sync if any constant's value changes later

2. Replace resolver type-ordering in prompt rendering with an explicit ordered list
    [x] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py': Swap alphabetical type sort for a fixed resolver precedence list
        - task: define a module-level TYPE_ORDER list (e.g. ManifestResolver, RepoContentResolver, MultiDocResolver) capturing intent instead of class-name alphabetics
        - task: rank resolvers by precedence using isinstance so PudBaseResolver/SharedBaseResolver subclasses fall into the MultiDoc slot (avoid .index() KeyError on subclass types)
        - task: apply that rank in the section sort (render_service.py, the section-sort step) replacing the current {type(r) for r in resolvers} alphabetical derivation
        - task: confirm the swap is intentional — repo and multidoc exchange positions relative to the previous alphabetical order
        - task: keep it scoped to render_service.py only; no other file encodes resolver ordering
        - prohibition: do not change dispatch order or section anchoring; only the within-section type ordering changes
        - prohibition: do not reorder across different anchors — precedence only reorders resolvers sharing one anchor

